{
  "summary": "Fixed bug in AgentSessionService where parseInt used wrong radix (3 instead of 10). The original code would fail to parse session limits like '10' correctly since radix 3 only allows digits 0-2.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "parseInt radix",
      "reminder": "Always use radix 10 for decimal numbers in parseInt. Other radix values (especially low ones like 3) will silently return NaN or incorrect values for digits outside that base."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Environment variable defaults",
      "reminder": "When using process.env with fallback defaults, verify the fallback value works correctly with the parsing logic. A value like '3' works for radix 3, but '10' does not."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Code review focus",
      "reminder": "Pay special attention to parsing functions - parseInt, Number(), etc. Incorrect radix in parseInt is a subtle but critical bug that compiles and passes type checking."
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Original code used radix 3 which only accepts digits 0-2. Any NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS value >= 3 would parse incorrectly or as NaN.",
      "location": "AgentSessionService.ts:24"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "priority": "medium",
      "description": "Add validation for NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS env var - ensure it's a positive integer within reasonable bounds (e.g., 1-100)"
    },
    {
      "priority": "low",
      "description": "Consider extracting the parseInt logic to a helper function to make the radix more visible and reduce repetition"
    }
  ],
  "praise": "The bug was caught during Inter-Review. The fix is minimal and correct - simply changing radix from 3 to 10.",
  "scores": {
    "overall": 85,
    "codeQuality": 90,
    "testCoverage": 70,
    "documentation": 80
  }
}

